exports[`what a shopper reads, state by state > checkFailed 1`] = `
"Product check
# We couldn't verify this tag
It didn't pass our check, so we can't confirm this product is authentic.
## What to do
- Tap the tag again
Hold the top of your phone on the tag for a second.
- Same result twice?
Treat the product as unverified. A copied or damaged tag fails this check.
- Tell the seller or the brand
An honest seller will want to know, and so will we.
Every authentic tag makes a new secret code on each tap. This one didn't pass.
[Report a problem → mailto:info@tagit.network?subject=A%20product%20check%20did%20not%20pass]
## How the check works
- Every tag proves itself
Each tap makes a one-time code that only the real tag can produce. A copy fails.
- Brands register each item
The check compares the tag with the brand's record of that exact item.
- Records can't be quietly changed
They are kept on a public ledger that anyone can inspect.
Pilot version. Records are kept on a public test network, and the system has not completed an external security audit.
[TAG IT Network → https://www.tagit.network]"
`;

